  'cold-plate':{chapter:'cooling',name:'Cold plate',description:'A thermally conductive plate sits against a chip. Coolant flowing through channels inside the plate carries the chip’s heat away.',path:'Chip → cold plate → warmer coolant → CDU',insight:'The coolant stays inside a sealed circuit. In this design, it does not flow freely over the electronic components.',source:doe},
